In $\text{KMnO}_4$, $\text{Mn}$ is in $+7$ oxidation state:
(i) $+7 \longrightarrow +6$ in $[\text{MnO}_4]^{2-}$: $1\;e^-$ transferred;
(ii) $+7 \longrightarrow +4$ in $\text{MnO}_2$: $3\;e^-$ transferred;
(iii) $+7 \longrightarrow +3$ in $\text{Mn}_2\text{O}_3$: $4\;e^-$ transferred;
(iv) $+7 \longrightarrow +2$ in $\text{Mn}^{2+}$: $5\;e^-$ transferred.
Thus, the numbers of electrons transferred are $1, 3, 4, 5$.

