(a) In $d$-block groups, higher oxidation states become more stable down the group, so $\text{W}(\text{VI})$ is more stable than $\text{Cr}(\text{VI})$ (Correct);
(b) Permanganate oxidises $\text{HCl}$ to $\text{Cl}_2$, giving unsatisfactory titration results (Incorrect);
(c) Certain lanthanoid oxides (e.g., $\text{Eu}_2\text{O}_3$) are used as phosphors in television screens (Correct).
Thus, only statement (b) is incorrect.

(a) $(\text{NH}_4)_2[\text{Ce}(\text{NO}_3)_6]$: $\text{Ce}^{4+}$ ($[\text{Xe}]4f^0$) $\rightarrow 0$ unpaired $e^-$, $\mu = 0\text{ BM}$;
(c) $\text{Eu}(\text{NO}_3)_3$: $\text{Eu}^{3+}$ ($[\text{Xe}]4f^6$) $\rightarrow 6$ unpaired $e^-$, $\mu = \sqrt{48}\text{ BM}$;
(b) $\text{Gd}(\text{NO}_3)_3$: $\text{Gd}^{3+}$ ($[\text{Xe}]4f^7$) $\rightarrow 7$ unpaired $e^-$, $\mu = \sqrt{63}\text{ BM}$.
Increasing order: $(a) < (c) < (b)$.

