In the T-shaped ($sp^3d$) structure of $\text{ClF}_3$, there are $n = 2$ lone pairs in the equatorial positions. Number of unpaired electrons:
(A) $\text{V}^{3+}$ ($3d^2$): $2$;
(B) $\text{Ti}^{3+}$ ($3d^1$): $1$;
(C) $\text{Cu}^{2+}$ ($3d^9$): $1$;
(D) $\text{Ni}^{2+}$ ($3d^8$): $2$;
(E) $\text{Ti}^{2+}$ ($3d^2$): $2$.
Thus, A, D and E Only.

$\mu = \sqrt{n(n+2)} = 4.9\text{ BM} \implies n = 4$ unpaired electrons.
(A) $\text{Cr}^{2+}$ ($[\text{Ar}]3d^4$): $4$ unpaired $e^-$;
(B) $\text{Fe}^{2+}$ ($[\text{Ar}]3d^6$): $4$ unpaired $e^-$;
(C) $\text{Fe}^{3+}$ ($[\text{Ar}]3d^5$): $5$ unpaired $e^-$;
(D) $\text{Co}^{2+}$ ($[\text{Ar}]3d^7$): $3$ unpaired $e^-$;
(E) $\text{Mn}^{3+}$ ($[\text{Ar}]3d^4$): $4$ unpaired $e^-$.
Thus, A, B and E only.

