In $\text{Cr}_2\text{O}_7^{2-}$, there are $6$ terminal oxygen atoms ($3$ on each $\text{Cr}$ atom) and $1$ bridging oxygen atom.

(A) In $\text{Mn}_2\text{O}_7$, $\text{Mn}$ is in its highest $+7$ oxidation state (Correct);
(B) Oxygen stabilises high oxidation states via $p\pi - d\pi$ multiple bonding (Correct);
(C) $\text{Mn}_2\text{O}_7$ is a covalent green oil, not an ionic oxide (Incorrect);
(D) $\text{O}_3\text{Mn}-\text{O}-\text{MnO}_3$ has one $\text{Mn}-\text{O}-\text{Mn}$ bridged oxygen atom (Correct).
Thus, A, B and D Only.

(A) Both $\text{MnO}_4^{2-}$ and $\text{MnO}_4^-$ have tetrahedral ($d^3s$) geometry (True);
(B) Oxidation state of $\text{Mn}$ is $+6$ in manganate and $+7$ in permanganate, not vice versa (False);
(C) Peroxodisulphate ($\text{S}_2\text{O}_8^{2-}$) oxidises $\text{Mn}^{2+}$ to permanganate ($\text{MnO}_4^-$), not manganate (False);
(D) $\text{MnO}_4^{2-}$ ($3d^1$) is paramagnetic and $\text{MnO}_4^-$ ($3d^0$) is diamagnetic (True);
(E) Acidified $\text{MnO}_4^-$ oxidises (not reduces) oxalate, nitrite, and iodide ions (False).
Thus, A and D Only.

(A) $\text{Mo}(\text{VI})$ and $\text{W}(\text{VI})$ are more stable than $\text{Cr}(\text{VI})$ (Incorrect);
(B) $\text{Ce}^{4+}$ and $\text{Tb}^{4+}$ tend to gain $1\;e^-$ to reach $+3$ (oxidants), while $\text{Eu}^{2+}$ and $\text{Yb}^{2+}$ tend to lose $1\;e^-$ to reach $+3$ (reductants) (Correct);
(C) $\text{Am}$ ($[\text{Rn}]5f^7 7s^2$) has $7$ unpaired $e^-$, while $\text{Cm}$ ($[\text{Rn}]5f^7 6d^1 7s^2$) has $8$ unpaired $e^-$ (Incorrect);
(D) Poorer shielding by $5f$ electrons causes greater element-to-element actinoid contraction than lanthanoid contraction (Correct).
Thus, B and D Only.

(A) Acidified $\text{K}_2\text{Cr}_2\text{O}_7$ oxidises $\text{Fe}^{2+}$ to $\text{Fe}^{3+}$ (Correct);
(B) $\text{Na}_2\text{Cr}_2\text{O}_7$ is deliquescent/hygroscopic and cannot be used as a primary standard (Incorrect);
(C) $2\text{CrO}_4^{2-} + 2\text{H}^+ \rightleftharpoons \text{Cr}_2\text{O}_7^{2-} + \text{H}_2\text{O}$ depends on solution $\text{pH}$ (Correct);
(D) The $\text{Cr}-\text{O}-\text{Cr}$ bond angle in $\text{Cr}_2\text{O}_7^{2-}$ is $126^\circ$ (Correct).
Thus, A, C and D Only.

Highest manganese fluoride is $\text{MnF}_4$ ($+4$) and highest manganese oxide is $\text{Mn}_2\text{O}_7$ ($+7$), so $|x| = |7 - 4| = 3$.
Number of unpaired electrons:
(A) $\text{Sc}^{3+}$ ($3d^0$): $0$;
(B) $\text{Zn}^{2+}$ ($3d^{10}$): $0$;
(C) $\text{V}^{2+}$ ($3d^3$): $3$;
(D) $\text{Fe}^{2+}$ ($3d^6$): $4$;
(E) $\text{Co}^{2+}$ ($3d^7$): $3$.
Thus, C and E Only.

Ground-state $4f$ electron counts:
$\text{Eu}$ ($[\text{Xe}]4f^7 6s^2$) and $\text{Gd}$ ($[\text{Xe}]4f^7 5d^1 6s^2$) both have $7$ electrons in $4f$ (A is correct);
$\text{Dy}$ ($4f^{10}$) and $\text{Ho}$ ($4f^{11}$) differ (B is incorrect);
$\text{Yb}$ ($[\text{Xe}]4f^{14}6s^2$) and $\text{Hf}$ ($[\text{Xe}]4f^{14}5d^2 6s^2$) both have $14$ electrons in $4f$ (C is correct);
$\text{Lu}$ ($4f^{14}$) and $\text{Tm}$ ($4f^{13}$) differ (D is incorrect).
Thus, A and C Only.

(A) $\text{V}_2\text{O}_5$ used in the Contact process is amphoteric, not basic (Incorrect);
(B) $\text{TiCl}_4$ used in Ziegler-Natta catalyst has $\text{Ti}^{4+}$ ($3d^0$), giving $\mu = 0\text{ BM}$ (Incorrect);
(C) $\text{Al}(\text{C}_2\text{H}_5)_3$ has $p$-block metal $\text{Al}$ in $+3$ oxidation state (Correct);
(D) $\text{PdCl}_2$ used in the Wacker process has $\text{Pd}^{2+}$ with $4d^8$ configuration ($8$ electrons in the outermost $d$ orbital) (Correct).
Thus, C and D Only.
